From 1d6994afd070c2fddfc3636ec6ee20fa34200b72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 23:11:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 286: the examiners were measuring themselves; replace them
 and unblind UNKNOWN

The first full --no-hidden run came back EVIDENCE_NO with LOO model 0.100 against
votes 0.014 and return 0.754, unknown_when_absent 0.000 against present 0.218,
and an exam of 0.777 against votes 0.932. Four of those five comparisons say
nothing about the mind.

1. The exam was a tautology. 280 defines item["truth"] as the majority value of
   the address, None on a tie; with every mention visible votes_judge computes
   exactly that function of exactly that input. votes WAS the label, and 0.9324
   is not a score but the ceiling - 21 clean + 6 decidable at 1.0 and 10 ties at
   the abstain reward is 34.5/37 to the digit. G_exam_matches_judges asked the
   mind to tie an oracle. Gate removed; the exam now reports oracle_reward and
   the gap to it, and gates on nothing.

2. Reward cannot tell silence from selectivity. At abstain +0.75 against wrong
   -1.0, answering beats silence only above 87.5% accuracy, so every scorer piles
   up on the constant. return_reward 0.7536 on n=70 admits nine integer solutions,
   from 1 item answered to 65, all at accuracy ~0.88: coverage was not in the
   number that was gating. Coverage, accuracy and reward are now reported apart
   for every scorer, the value of unconditional silence is printed beside them,
   and a judge under 10% coverage is marked vacuous rather than beaten or lost to
   (JUDGES_VACUOUS is a verdict now).

3. The comparison had no direction. The model answered 58 of 70 at 0.483; the
   return judge answered few at ~0.88. G_learns_evidence now ranks items by the
   mind's own confidence, cuts at the JUDGE's coverage, and compares accuracy
   there. Still relative, still no constant to pick.

4. UNKNOWN at the argmax fights the base rate, and in the regime that dominated
   training it was not predictable at all. Whether the hidden value appears among
   the visible ones is a property of the HIDDEN slot; where the evidence is
   unanimous the UNKNOWN row is [1/n, 1.0, 1/n, 1.0] under both labels, so the
   21% absent rate is irreducible noise there and "never say UNKNOWN" is the
   optimal response. 0.000 was correct behaviour. Honesty is now measured in the
   distribution: AUC of P(UNKNOWN) separating absent from present, with the argmax
   rates kept as diagnostics.

Two defects in the head, both of which the ablation exposed by failing:

5. The UNKNOWN row was blind to corroboration. Its four features were
   [1/n, margin, n_distinct/n, flag] while a candidate's third feature was its
   external support - so the row that decides whether to answer at all could not
   see the one signal saying whether any candidate deserves an answer, and the
   head could not express the return judge's rule while holding the return
   judge's feature. That gap is the whole of 0.100 against 0.754. Every row now
   carries the same schema: four own numbers plus five example-level numbers
   (n_distinct/n, lead margin, 1/n, best external support, its margin) broadcast
   to all rows, UNKNOWN included.

6. Truncation mislabelled the target. cands is most_common(8); a target present
   in the evidence but ranked ninth was labelled UNKNOWN - label noise pointing
   the wrong way on exactly the axis gate 4 measures. Presence is decided against
   the full counter, truncated examples are dropped from training and counted.

Also measured now because it was invisible: the training distribution. Six of the
eight logged steps had one candidate while the held-out tape had 3.56, so the mind
trained in the copying regime and was scored outside it. train_distribution is
reported and G_task_exists gates on it; --min-candidates can exclude the unanimous
regime for an arm that wants only the weighing task.

Consequence for the record: the --no-hidden arm has no verdict yet. It was scored
by examiners that no longer exist and must be rerun before the hidden arm means
anything.

Unrelated, found while reading: _stage280_raw_exam.py referenced args.addr_key and
args.run_tag without declaring either, so it died in argparse when run standalone
(286 only imports pack_from_corpus and never hit it). Both flags added, and
run_tag now reaches the filename tag as the baseline invocation in HANDOFF.md
assumes.

Verified without torch or the corpus: a stubbed self-test exercises example(),
scorer_stats(), acc_at_coverage() and auc(), confirms the shared feature schema
and the UNKNOWN row's view of support, and re-derives 0.9324 as the exam ceiling
and the nine solutions behind 0.7536.

