+  "note": "The direction of teaching is inverted: nobody demonstrates, the tape is the label. Hide one mention of an address, show the rest, require the hidden value - so there are as many examples as slots, no judge is imitated, and what the weights learn is what the judges were hand-written approximations of: weighing evidence. Votes and corroboration are features on the candidates now, and each candidate is READ from the mentions that carry it - a single pooled vector would have been the same for every row and could not have said which candidate the text supports. UNKNOWN is a candidate whose target is real whenever the hidden value is absent from the visible evidence, so honesty is trained rather than assumed, and the answer is the argmax - no threshold anywhere. Scored on a tape from a disjoint corpus by three relative examiners: beat both hand-written judges at leave-one-out, say UNKNOWN more when the answer is absent than when it is present, and keep beating votes when one visible mention is forged. The lying tape is the test that judgment lives in reading, not in the parameters: the forged mention has no external corroboration and a mind that weighs evidence should discount it, while votes by construction cannot. The address itself is still 280's plumbing - this stage is about weighing WITHIN the evidence set, and the candidate list is what the evidence says, so the ceiling here is what a correct address makes visible.",
